      "rev_n_1_f720ed_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_f720ed_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_f720ed",
        "thought_text": "The operation repeatedly reduces N by subtracting K until N is less than K, then it starts increasing N back towards K. The minimum value occurs when N is closest to K modulo K.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794392379.2287161
      },
      "rev_n_2_2b0b8e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_2b0b8e_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_2b0b8e",
        "thought_text": "Consider the properties of absolute differences. If N is greater than K, the first operation will reduce N by at least K. If N is less than K, the first operation will increase N. The pattern suggests that the minimum value is the remainder of N divided by K.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794392379.228752
      },
      "rev_n_3_4511d9_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_4511d9_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_4511d9",
        "thought_text": "Simulate the operation iteratively starting from N and observe the pattern of values taken. The sequence will eventually stabilize around a small set of numbers, including the minimum possible value.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794392379.228778
      },
      "rev_n_4_140127_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_140127_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_140127",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of using N % K might be incorrect because it doesn't account for the possibility of N being larger than K initially. We need to consider both the cases where N is greater than K and where N is less than K.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1453225575795091102",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794392410.437336
      },
      "rev_n_5_2a47da_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_2a47da_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_2a47da",
        "thought_text": "A potential issue could be that the operation might not always reduce N to the minimum possible value in one step. We should consider the sequence of operations and how they affect the value of N over multiple steps.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "1453225575795091102",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794392410.4374459
      },
      "rev_n_6_c86ce9_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_c86ce9_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_c86ce9",
        "thought_text": "We should verify the logic by considering edge cases, such as when N is equal to K, or when N is much larger than K. This will help us understand if our current approach is missing any crucial conditions.",
